# Tauri dev watcher exclusions.
#
# We run the standalone backend (ao-server) outside of `tauri dev` during
# working sessions so SSE streams and in-memory state survive across iterations.
# That means rebuilding the Tauri-embedded copy of the engine on every edit to
# `crates/` is pure waste — it tears down the Tauri shell (and the WebView with
# it) without changing what the standalone BE is serving.
#
# Patterns use .gitignore syntax and are matched against paths within the
# Cargo workspace that Tauri's file watcher traverses. Keep this list tight:
# anything ignored here will NOT trigger a Tauri rebuild, so only add paths
# that are genuinely irrelevant to the Tauri shell binary itself.
#
# Still watched (intentional):
#   - src-tauri/src/**        Tauri shell code: IPC commands, window setup, etc.
#   - src-tauri/Cargo.toml    Shell dependency changes.
#   - src-tauri/build.rs      Shell build script.

# Engine + tool crates — owned by the standalone BE in dev.
crates/

# Workspace integration tests — never linked into the Tauri shell.
tests/

# Workspace lockfile — flips on any dep bump anywhere in the workspace
# and would otherwise force a full Tauri rebuild for unrelated changes.
Cargo.lock
